{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles","id":1406204,"title":"Autochthonia and vehicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-03T18:59:19-07:00","id":1406204,"title":"Autochthonia and vehicles","content":"With 3rd Edition trying to move away somewhat from magitech and move artifacts toward being more rare, I had some thoughts about Autochthonia and vehciles that I wanted to share and see what other people thought.<br /> <br /> Autochthonia, with its somewhere-between-steampunk-and-techno-futurism aesthetic, made plenty of use of various artifact vehicles in 2nd edition, powering them with elemental cores and putting them in the hands of mortals of high rank and the military. With the typical such vehicle being rated somewhere around 4 dots, it made for quite a few potent artifacts lying around. To keep the aesthetic of hover cars, transport crawlers, and tunnel trams, perhaps what we'll see is that most such vehicles will be powered by one or more Municipal Alchemical Charms, such as a train station or an airport. The actual vehicles, rather than being made from the Magical Materials, would be ordinary steel, copper, and aluminum and tap into an energy field broadcast by the patropolis. With &quot;mundane&quot; vehicles in existence, artifact versions can then be special, custom-made creations intended for use by Champions.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T19:21:10-07:00","id":1406205,"title":"","content":"I'd go even simpler.<br /> Mundane autochtonian vehicles are powered by fuel. Common fuel, mostly extracted from the dregs of the titan's world-body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T21:06:29-07:00","id":1406212,"title":"","content":"Honestly I feel that Autochthonia shouldn't change too much. It's explicitly the weird clockwork and steampunk alternate setting, it should be allowed to get a little wilder than Creation proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T23:06:26-07:00","id":1406223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles?p=1406205#post1406205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go even simpler.<br /> Mundane autochtonian vehicles are powered by fuel. Common fuel, mostly extracted from the dregs of the titan's world-body.</div> </div> </div> </div>This causes versimulitude issues during games where the Seal of Eight Divinities is broken. If flying machines just need gas in the tank, why hasn't at least cars or trains become a thing in Creation yet? The ancient Greeks were beginning to experiment with the steam engine and they didn't have magical geniuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T04:31:11-07:00","id":1406250,"title":"","content":"It might simply be a limitation of paradigm. First Age craft is dissonant with creation even if it were to be mundane, whereas that doesn't make sense in autochtonia.<br /> It might be a limitation of what &quot;fuel&quot; stands for. Autochtonia is its own world, and maybe materials natural to it are conducive for mass produced vehicles. You can call it magic, but it's really the kind of magic that muddles with the mundane, much like Creation's little magics and wards, and thus doesn't deserve much more consideration than that. <br /> If vehicles are still supposed to be wondrous and unique, at least from a mortal perspective, then we are back to artifacts and charm-backed pseudo-artifacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T05:55:30-07:00","id":1406258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles?p=1406223#post1406223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This causes versimulitude issues during games where the Seal of Eight Divinities is broken. If flying machines just need gas in the tank, why hasn't at least cars or trains become a thing in Creation yet? The ancient Greeks were beginning to experiment with the steam engine and they didn't have magical geniuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation <i>does</i> have flying vehichles that just need gas in the tank; haslanti airboats run on kerosene. Why (insert technology here) hasn't been invented yet in Creation even though there are all these magical geniuses running around is a well-debated topic.<br /> <br /> That said I do agree witb your original thesis, to a point. Given 3e's new attitude to artifacts some rebalancing of dot ratings is probably in order. Also, I think leaving the vehicles as proper artifacts is fine, but you'll need some sort of mechanical hook explaining why crafting them is so much easier in Autochthonia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 08-04-2020, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T05:58:36-07:00","id":1406259,"title":"","content":"I've previously mused that elementals could be a major factor in Autochthonian transportation if you wanted to dial back the super technology in favour of them being people in an alien world that happens to look like super technology.<br /> <br /> I guess it depends on where Ex3 goes with them. Their historical symbiosis with the Alchemical Exalted has been one of the strongest reasons to downplay their impact upon the rest of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T06:39:59-07:00","id":1406260,"title":"","content":"Perhaps autochthonia has electric trains that are forced to snake between conduits to the pole of lightning on their way to their destinations.<br /> <br /> A lot of the differences in tech could be down to the vastly different natural resources available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T12:51:24-07:00","id":1406317,"title":"","content":"There is also the tools to make the tools and the infrastructure issues. A perfectly functional car factory in the age of sorrows will not produce any cars. There are no roads for those cars to drive on, no roads to connect it to the rest of the supply chain (which also doesn't exist), no demand, no pool of sufficiently trained craftspeople to draw from that will accept a profitable wage, etc.<br /> <br /> Vehicles are the keystone of an arch, and the rest of the blocks were thrown down and broken into gravel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T15:07:01-07:00","id":1406335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles?p=1406258#post1406258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creation <i>does</i> have flying vehichles that just need gas in the tank; haslanti airboats run on kerosene. Why (insert technology here) hasn't been invented yet in Creation even though there are all these magical geniuses running around is a well-debated topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haslanti airboats, though, are very different from a shaft speeder, which was a nod to the Nebuchadnezzar from the Matrix.<br /> <br /> I never picked up CoTD: The North, so I don't know a huge amount about the Haslanti. When you say they &quot;run on kerosene&quot;, do you mean they heat the gasbag using kerosene or do you mean they have some form of kerosene-powered engine, because those two things have majorly different implications. The first just implies they have a source of lamp and heating oil like the ancient Chinese did. The second implies the North's on the verge of major cultural and infrastructural upheaval that will spread across Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T21:22:43-07:00","id":1406378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles?p=1406335#post1406335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Haslanti airboats, though, are very different from a shaft speeder, which was a nod to the Nebuchadnezzar from the Matrix.<br /> <br /> I never picked up CoTD: The North, so I don't know a huge amount about the Haslanti. When you say they &amp;quot;run on kerosene&amp;quot;, do you mean they heat the gasbag using kerosene or do you mean they have some form of kerosene-powered engine, because those two things have majorly different implications. The first just implies they have a source of lamp and heating oil like the ancient Chinese did. The second implies the North's on the verge of major cultural and infrastructural upheaval that will spread across Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Airboats use their fuel for lift, yes. But the key thing is actually that the fuel is *kerosene*. Kerosene is what we use now for jet fuel. In our world, kerosene was invented 50 years or so after the internal combustion engine. It's a major step forward in energy availability, lighting, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, I was more bringing it up as a &quot;non-artifact vehicle&quot; reference point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T02:01:54-07:00","id":1406399,"title":"","content":"I would be reluctant to change Autocthonia to make it fit &quot;Better&quot; with creation. That, IMO, simply leaves fans of Autocthon and fans of creation-based games, equally unhappy. I'd prefer to just play up the fact that Autocthonia <i>isn't</i> mandated to appear in creation, leaving you free to play in a very different environment, while leaving some suggestions on how to handle contact, with the cavaet that it would be a big, big deal, and represent a change to creation easily as big as the fall of the Shogunate or the Usurpation. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T04:21:42-07:00","id":1406409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles#post1406204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With 3rd Edition trying to move away somewhat from magitech and move artifacts toward being more rare, I had some thoughts about Autochthonia and vehciles that I wanted to share and see what other people thought.<br /> <br /> Autochthonia, with its somewhere-between-steampunk-and-techno-futurism aesthetic, made plenty of use of various artifact vehicles in 2nd edition, powering them with elemental cores and putting them in the hands of mortals of high rank and the military. With the typical such vehicle being rated somewhere around 4 dots, it made for quite a few potent artifacts lying around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arms of the Chosen still has the Chariot of Aerial Conquest. Such vehicles are still perfectly in keeping with the vanilla setting, let alone Autochthonia.<br /> <br /> It's not as if the Octet ever had vast fleets of the things; they lack the space or the personnel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To keep the aesthetic of hover cars, transport crawlers, and tunnel trams, perhaps what we'll see is that most such vehicles will be powered by one or more Municipal Alchemical Charms, such as a train station or an airport. The actual vehicles, rather than being made from the Magical Materials, would be ordinary steel, copper, and aluminum and tap into an energy field broadcast by the patropolis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the trams were already supposed to be things that mostly just went with the flow of the Maker's internal tubing, with the occasional polis hooked into them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-05T10:13:17-07:00","id":1406459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles?p=1406378#post1406378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Airboats use their fuel for lift, yes. But the key thing is actually that the fuel is *kerosene*. Kerosene is what we use now for jet fuel. In our world, kerosene was invented 50 years or so after the internal combustion engine. It's a major step forward in energy availability, lighting, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first record of the distillation of kerosene was written in the 9th century, about a thousand years before the invention of the internal combustion engine. The Chinese were using it as a lamp fuel during the Ming Dynasty. Easier processes for the production of kerosene, first from coal and then from petroleum, is one of the things that contributed to the end of commercial whaling, but it was an increase in convenience rather than a breakthrough in terms of energy density. Oil doesn't run away like whales do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, I was more bringing it up as a &quot;non-artifact vehicle&quot; reference point. </div> </div> </div>It's a good reference point, but I think it demonstrates just how huge the gulf between Autochthonian transportation technology and Creation's transportation technology is. The Haslanti have fragile dirigibles, the Autochthonians have armored, self-propelled airships.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles?p=1406399#post1406399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be reluctant to change Autocthonia to make it fit &quot;Better&quot; with creation. That, IMO, simply leaves fans of Autocthon and fans of creation-based games, equally unhappy. I'd prefer to just play up the fact that Autocthonia <i>isn't</i> mandated to appear in creation, leaving you free to play in a very different environment, while leaving some suggestions on how to handle contact, with the cavaet that it would be a big, big deal, and represent a change to creation easily as big as the fall of the Shogunate or the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to make it fit Creation &quot;better&quot; per se. I'm seeing a trend in the game line as a whole that I assume will naturally include Autocthonia, with characters possessing fewer artifacts, the number of artifacts in the setting being played down, while the impact of individual artifacts played up. A concentration of narrative weight, if you will. The game's mechanics already incentivize taking a single daiklave and buying several of its Evocations instead of buying the broader artifact panoply of 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> Maintaining the Autochhonian aesthetic while allowing this sort of change to the prevalence of artifacts requires the offloading of some of those elements from artifacts and onto something else. Luckily for us, Autochthonia has something that can easily shoulder that load in the form of patropoli and metropoli. That such an explanation also prevents one of the Eight Nations from becoming an instant world power beyond the capacity of Lookshy during a &quot;Breach of the Seal of Eight Divinities&quot; scenario is more a happy bonus than a primary goal.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1406204-autochthonia-and-vehicles?p=1406409#post1406409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arms of the Chosen still has the Chariot of Aerial Conquest. Such vehicles are still perfectly in keeping with the vanilla setting, let alone Autochthonia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying that such vehicles will cease to exist. The apparent trend is that artifacts will be rarer and certainly won't be the &quot;mass-produced in the First Age&quot; magitech creations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not as if the Octet ever had vast fleets of the things; they lack the space or the personnel. </div> </div> </div>Nurad at the least had a significant number. Air superiority is one of those things that dramatically altered the nature of warfare and Creation isn't a world of tight tunnels that limits the advantages that air power can bring to bear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the trams were already supposed to be things that mostly just went with the flow of the Maker's internal tubing, with the occasional polis hooked into them. </div> </div> </div>Outside cities, sure. Inside cities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-06T10:41:22-07:00","id":1406648,"title":"","content":"This is the kind of thing I'm getting at for suggesting Elementals could take the place of vehicles.<br /> <br /> They look like advanced mecha but the crew being in a howdah suggests that they didn't design these robots and don't trust them to act autonamously, making them Autochthonian war elephants, so to speak.<br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/71/29/59/7129594ce2d66ff52df18777f783c4eb.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T21:34:29-07:00","id":1409283,"title":"","content":"I can very much imagine Autochtonian metal elementals being like that, or with a bunch of weirder body plans.<br /> Let's just say it's one of those the natives are more comfortable having a howdah to guide - and use ranged attacks of their own - from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}